+/// §16 Part B: the segments of a routed keep-down travel that replaces the
+/// entry `entry` (`keep_down_route`), or `None`: the travel is off, the
+/// tool has no position, or no route holds.
+///
+/// - The travel runs at the entry's Z (cut feed: `Link`s, free cells to the
+///   stay-down clearance above it) or at the entry's Z plus the rapid
+///   clearance (rapid: `LowRapid`s, free cells to that clearance). Either
+///   way a free cell's whole tool disc stands at most the clearance above
+///   the travel's floor: the full-disc proof.
+/// - §16.7: only an entry whose own disc is free (it cuts nothing) is
+///   replaced: a keep-down travel replaces the travel, never the entry's
+///   cut. The route ends on the entry, with no side leg.
